        <mxCell id="l8" value="reset main to previous&lt;br&gt;release tag, re-Update&lt;br&gt;Shared WS" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;dashed=1;strokeColor=#8c8c8c;fontColor=#4d4d4d;exitX=1;exitY=0.4;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.22;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n30" target="n21"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as='points'><mxPoint x="1180" y="3643"/><mxPoint x="1180" y="2245"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l9" value="fix forward on a&lt;br&gt;fresh feature branch" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;dashed=1;strokeColor=#8c8c8c;fontColor=#4d4d4d;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.7;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n30" target="n9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as='points'><mxPoint x="745" y="3655"/><mxPoint x="745" y="320"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e29" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n31" target="n32"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g10" value="hand-off" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;dashed=1;strokeColor=#8c8c8c;fontColor=#4d4d4d;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n31" target="offpage"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e30" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n32" target="end"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l10" value="Feedback &amp;#8594; backlog&lt;br&gt;(next iteration)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;dashed=1;strokeColor=#8c8c8c;fontColor=#4d4d4d;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.9;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n32" target="n9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as='points'><mxPoint x="700" y="3915"/><mxPoint x="700" y="340"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legendBox" value="Legend &amp;#8212; Operational Domain" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="1560" width="560" height="175" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg0" value="CC / VSC on Local Files" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="15" y="40" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg1" value="CC via MCP against Fabric" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="290" y="40" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg2" value="Fabric Web UI &amp;#8212; sole activity surface" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="15" y="76" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg3" value="Local Git / Mixed (Git &amp;#183; ADO &amp;#183; Fabric &amp;#183; CC)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="290" y="76" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg4" value="Azure DevOps (ADO) &amp;#8212; sole activity surface" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="15" y="112" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg5" value="Decision Gateway" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="290" y="112" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legPhase" value="Solid dark-grey border = phase boundary &amp;#183; dashed grey arrow = feedback / rollback path" style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="15" y="146" width="530" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="abbrevBox" value="Key &amp;#8212; Abbreviations" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="1780" width="560" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="abbrevL" value="ADO &amp;#8212; Azure DevOps&lt;br&gt;ADR &amp;#8212; Architecture Decision Record&lt;br&gt;API &amp;#8212; Application Programming Interface&lt;br&gt;CC &amp;#8212; Claude Code (CLI)&lt;br&gt;CLI &amp;#8212; Command-Line Interface&lt;br&gt;Ctx &amp;#8212; Context: active Fabric WS / Git branch&lt;br&gt;DAX &amp;#8212; Data Analysis Expressions&lt;br&gt;Fab &amp;#8212; Fabric (commit-message prefix)&lt;br&gt;JSON &amp;#8212; JavaScript Object Notation&lt;br&gt;MCP &amp;#8212; Model Context Protocol&lt;br&gt;OLS &amp;#8212; Object-Level Security&lt;br&gt;PR &amp;#8212; Pull Request" style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="abbrevBox"><mxGeometry x="12" y="34" width="268" height="196" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="abbrevR" value="QA &amp;#8212; Quality Assurance&lt;br&gt;RBAC &amp;#8212; Role-Based Access Control&lt;br&gt;REST &amp;#8212; Representational State Transfer&lt;br&gt;RLS &amp;#8212; Row-Level Security&lt;br&gt;SC &amp;#8212; Source Control (Fabric panel)&lt;br&gt;SDLC &amp;#8212; Software Development Life Cycle&lt;br&gt;SHA &amp;#8212; Secure Hash Algorithm (commit hash)&lt;br&gt;SQL &amp;#8212; Structured Query Language&lt;br&gt;T-SQL &amp;#8212; Transact-SQL&lt;br&gt;TMDL &amp;#8212; Tabular Model Definition Language&lt;br&gt;VSC &amp;#8212; Visual Studio Code&lt;br&gt;WS &amp;#8212; Workspace" style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="abbrevBox"><mxGeometry x="290" y="34" width="258" height="196" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notesBox" value="Notes (cited in steps as ᵃ ᵇ ᶜ &amp;#8230;)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="2055" width="560" height="1800" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notesText" value="&lt;b&gt;a&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Spec templates: reusable Markdown skeletons (ADR, source-to-target mapping, measure definitions, pipeline specs) generated via CC CLI to standardise design documentation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;b&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Branch strategy: main + short-lived feature branches only. Test/Prod content is delivered by Deployment Pipelines, not Git &amp;#8212; no test/prod branches exist; Git binding applies only to Dev-stage workspaces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;c&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Shared Integration/Dev WS: bound to main and doubles as the Deployment Pipeline Dev stage. Personal Dev WSs are branched workspaces sitting outside the deployment pipeline.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;d&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Branch-out: Fabric&amp;#8217;s &amp;#8220;Branch out to new workspace&amp;#8221; creates both the branch and the workspace bound to it &amp;#8212; no pre-created local branch is needed; the local fetch/checkout follows at Step 11. Item definitions are copied, but data source bindings are not retargeted &amp;#8212; repoint them at the Personal WS. Data is not copied either: lakehouses and warehouses in the branched workspace arrive empty, so re-create shortcuts and run the ingestion pipelines (Step 17) before validating.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;e&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; No auto-commit: Fabric Git Integration never commits automatically; a manual Source Control &amp;#8594; Commit is always required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Sync rule: local edits are invisible to Fabric until pushed to ADO and pulled via workspace &amp;#8220;Update&amp;#8221;. MCP always operates on workspace state, never local files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;g&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Validation loop: MCP-driven smoke tests in the Personal WS &amp;#8212; pipeline runs on sample data, Livy row-count checks, validation DAX vs expected results, semantic model refresh without errors, and &amp;#8220;View as role&amp;#8221; RLS/OLS checks per note ˣ &amp;#8212; before any PR.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;h&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Commit/PR message body: [domain]_[artifact]_[action]; PRs merge feature &amp;#8594; main with peer review.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;i&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Automation candidate: the manual WS &amp;#8220;Update&amp;#8221; is a single-owner action today; automatable via the Fabric Git REST API.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;j&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Deployment Pipelines &amp;#8212; one-off setup (outside the release loop): create the deployment pipeline and assign the Dev/Test/Prod workspaces to stages. Per release, pipelines copy item structure and metadata only: data does not deploy, and data source bindings are not retargeted automatically. Environment-specific values are supplied by the Variable Library (note ʷ); Deployment Rules remain the fallback for anything the Variable Library does not cover.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;k&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Report hand-off: reports are authored in the Fabric Web UI directly against the endorsed Prod semantic model, and the report artifacts are stored in the Prod workspace. The report authoring SDLC is deliberately out of scope here and will be fine-tuned in a later revision.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;l&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Release tag: tag the exact commit that was deployed to Test &amp;#8212; not simply the newest commit on main, which may have moved on. Do this in ADO: Azure Repos &amp;#8594; Tags &amp;#8594; New tag, selecting that commit (e.g. release/v1.2) &amp;#8212; the same surface as the PR, so the deployed SHA is chosen explicitly. Because the Prod WS is not Git-bound, the tag is the authoritative record of what is deployed to Prod, and is what a Prod rollback resets to (note ᶻ). Reserve scripted git tag / push --tags for release automation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;m&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Commit prefixes by surface: local VSC: &amp;#8220;VSC Commit: &amp;lt;msg&amp;gt;&amp;#8221; &amp;#183; local CC: &amp;#8220;CC Commit: &amp;lt;msg&amp;gt;&amp;#8221; &amp;#183; ADO web: &amp;#8220;ADO Commit: &amp;lt;msg&amp;gt;&amp;#8221; &amp;#183; Fabric UI: &amp;#8220;Fab Commit: &amp;lt;msg&amp;gt;&amp;#8221;. Message body follows note ʰ.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;n&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Rollback on main: if merged changes fail integration validation, restore main to a known-good state rather than fixing forward on a broken main. Done entirely in ADO &amp;#8212; Revert on the merged PR (equivalent to git revert -m 1 &amp;lt;merge-SHA&amp;gt;) and complete the revert PR. Two follow-on actions: re-Update the Shared Integration WS (Step 21) to pull the restored state, and re-work the defect from Step 9 on a fresh feature branch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;o&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Pre-PR sync: before raising the PR, fetch and merge (or rebase onto) main and resolve conflicts locally in VSC. TMDL and pipeline JSON conflicts must be resolved as text locally &amp;#8212; Fabric cannot resolve them.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;p&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Cleanup: after a validated merge, delete the feature branch in ADO and delete (or unbind) the Personal Dev WS. Prevents orphaned branched workspaces and stale branch bindings accumulating.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;r&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Endorsement: promotion / certification is item metadata that is NOT carried by Deployment Pipelines. It must be re-applied manually on the Prod semantic model after each promotion, and certification requires a tenant-designated certifier.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;s&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; MCP write rule: MCP acts on workspace state, not local files, so anything it creates bypasses Git and PR review until someone manually commits it in Fabric &amp;#8212; repo/workspace drift stays invisible until then. Standing rule: MCP is run / read / validate only (Steps 17, 18, 22, 29, 32). Item definitions are authored locally as TMDL, T-SQL and pipeline JSON (Steps 13&amp;#8211;14) and reach Fabric via Git. Step 6 is the sole, one-off exception: empty shells seed an otherwise empty repo.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;t&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Requirements as artifacts: ADRs, source-to-target mappings and measure definitions live as versioned Markdown in the repo, not as one-off documents. Step 1 is one-off inception; Step 9 is the recurring re-entry point where specs are refined at the head of every iteration and merged through the same PR as the code they describe. All feedback and defect loops return here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;u&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Plan Mode: CC plan mode proposes an implementation plan without writing to disk. No local authoring begins until the plan is approved, so intent is agreed before code exists; the approved plan is committed into the spec set (note ᵗ) and versioned alongside the change it produced.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;v&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Connections &amp;amp; shortcuts: source connections, gateways and OneLake shortcuts are workspace/tenant-level objects created once during setup. They are not versioned in Git and are not carried by Deployment Pipelines &amp;#8212; recreate or rebind them per stage (see notes ʲ and ʷ).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;w&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Variable Library: a first-class Fabric item, Git-versioned like any other, holding environment-specific values (lakehouse IDs, connection references, parameters) as named value sets. Scaffold it with the other shells at Step 6 with one value set per stage; each deployment-pipeline stage then activates its own set, so no hard-coded IDs travel between Dev, Test and Prod. The active value set is stage configuration rather than part of the item definition, so it is not overwritten on deployment &amp;#8212; confirm it explicitly at each promotion.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;x&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; RLS / OLS: row- and object-level security roles are part of the semantic model definition and live in TMDL, so they are authored, committed and PR-reviewed like any other code (Step 14) and tested with &amp;#8220;View as role&amp;#8221; in the Personal Dev WS before the PR. Role membership is a separate, per-workspace assignment (note ʸ) and is not carried by Deployment Pipelines.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;y&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Capacity &amp;amp; access &amp;#8212; two distinct concerns, deliberately placed at opposite ends of the flow. Capacity assignment is infrastructure: every workspace must be bound to a Fabric capacity (F-SKU or trial) at Step 3, or Spark, Direct Lake and Deployment Pipelines will not function. RBAC role assignment is an identity question that is often unsettled at inception, so Prod workspace roles and RLS role membership are assigned at Step 27, immediately before the Test &amp;#8594; Prod promotion.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;z&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; &amp;#8212; Prod verification &amp;amp; rollback: Fabric has no one-click Prod rollback. If post-deployment verification fails, reset main to the previous release tag (note ˡ), re-Update the Shared Integration WS and re-promote through the Deployment Pipeline &amp;#8212; a full cycle, not a rollback button. Where the defect is understood, fixing forward from Step 9 on a fresh feature branch is often faster; choose deliberately rather than by default." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="notesBox"><mxGeometry x="10" y="36" width="540" height="1750" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>